  "notes": "Historical catalog year, built for the parallel per-year build-out (see docs/BRANCH_CAMPUS_FINDINGS.md for the methodology). Fetched the real archived 2024-25 bulletin page (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/health-human-development/hospitality-management-bs/) and cross-checked its raw HTML 'sc_plangrid' table row by row (not WebFetch's summary alone) against both the 2025-26 archive and the live 2026-27 page; all three years' semester credit subtotals were confirmed to sum to each page's own stated per-term total before use. Real, confirmed difference found: the 2024-25 Suggested Academic Plan's Second Year Spring term explicitly REQUIRES 'HM 290W' (Hospitality Managerial Communication, 3cr) as a named course -- e.g. 'HM 290W *' alongside HM 336 and HM 280 -- whereas the 2025-26 and 2026-27 plans no longer list HM 290W anywhere in their required sequence at all (confirmed absent from both the 2025-26 archive and the live page's full course-code list) and instead fill that same credit slot with a generic HM Elective. Modeled here by substituting one of 2025's/2026's two Semester-4 generic 'HM Elective' slots with an explicit required 'HM 290W' item (same 3-credit value, no net credit change) -- this is a real course-code difference, not an approximation. HM 290W is not in this app's hm_catalog.json (it predates the current scraped catalog, same situation as HM 297S/HM 442/HM 265 below), so it schedules prereq-unchecked, same convention already used for Gen Ed slot-type items elsewhere in this plan; this is safe here since nothing in the 2024-25 sequence lists HM 290W as anyone else's prerequisite. Everything else in the sequence (First Year, Second Year Fall, Third Year, Fourth Year) is byte-for-byte identical to 2025-26/2026-27 -- same courses, same credits, same semester placement, confirmed by direct diff of the full course-code lists scraped from all three archived/live pages. Retained HM-2026.json's own two documented catalog-driven fixes unchanged, since the shared hm_catalog.json's course descriptions/prereqs apply to every catalog year regardless of which year's flowchart literally prints: the explicit 'HM 201' item in Semester 5 (HM 366's real prereq), and the HM 490->HM 490W substitution (HM 492's real prereq is HM 430 AND HM 490W; the 2024-25 flowchart, like every other year checked, literally prints plain 'HM 490' with no W). Campus availability: the 2024-25 archive's own campus toggle reads identically to 2025-26/2026-27 -- End Campus 'University Park' only, Berks listed separately for the different Hospitality Entrepreneurship option; Erie (Behrend) and Brandywine are not offered for this program in this year either.",
